{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, PCA n2000 + ResNet50, concat) is the best result so far (acc 0.527, F1 0.510), showing a modest ~4pp gain over RNA-alone (0.485). All completed experiments use singleprofile; the multiprofile + aggregation axis is completely untested and represents a major design uncertainty. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) in the multimodal setting improve over the single-profile baseline, and if so, by how much? Why this config: config_018 is the minimal, direct extension of the current best (config_016) along the single untested dimension (profile/aggregation), keeping RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy identical. This isolates the multiprofile+avgpool effect, reducing uncertainty about whether profile aggregation is worth the added complexity before investing further experiments in transformer aggregation or alternative fusion. Under a tight budget, this one experiment tells us whether the multiprofile axis is worth exploring at all, making it the highest-information next step."
}

